<title>USA: Wells Fargo stock seen sharply lower.</title>
<headline>Wells Fargo stock seen sharply lower.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-07-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Wells Fargo and Co was expected to open as much as $25 a share lower Wednesday after the company issued a warning of an earnings shortfall, traders said.</p>
<p>George Salem, analyst at Gerard Klauer Mattison, said with no conference call with analysts scheduled until June 16, the day after the detailed earnings release, &quot;it looks like there is going to be a gap here where the stock will drift.&quot;</p>
<p>Wells Fargo closed Tuesday at 279.</p>
</text>
